   "mechanism": "TREM2–DAP12 signaling recruits a phosphoinositide signaling program in which PLCG2 generates DAG and IP3, while INPP5D/SHIP1 removes PIP3 and dampens PI3K signaling. Alzheimer risk reflects an improperly tuned signaling set point: insufficient PLCG2 output or excessive INPP5D braking reduces calcium-dependent chemotaxis, endocytosis, and plaque compaction, whereas the PLCG2 protective allele shifts the system toward a productive response.",
